# OS / editor junk
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*~

# Dependencies + build scratch
node_modules/
tools/node_modules/
tools/*.json
out/
*.log

# Backups of the pre-optimisation media (keep them out of the repo)
*.orig
*.bak
*-backup.*
assets-original/

# VIDEO MASTERS. 1.mp4, 3.mp4 and 4.mp4 are the H.264 sources the shipped VP9
# scenes were encoded from. Nothing in the book ever requests them — the deploy
# already strips them (see .vercelignore) — but they were still TRACKED, so they
# travelled with the repo: 18.6 MB of a 35.4 MB tree, and 56% of the GitHub
# "Download ZIP", for files no visitor can reach.
# Untracked rather than deleted: they stay on the machine that builds the book, so
# the scenes can be re-encoded from source. Measured before doing this — the
# shipped encodes are within ~1.3 VMAF of anything a higher bitrate can buy from
# these masters, so nothing of value is waiting to be recovered from them.
FLIPBOOK/assets/*.mp4
